      "name": {
        "name": "Nucleolar protein 4 family",
        "short": "NOL4/NOL4L"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>NOL4 has been identified as a methylation target for cervical [[cite:PUB00083195]] and head and neck cancer [[cite:PUB00083196]]. NOL4L was first identified in acute myeloid leukaemia and was shown to be involved in cell progression in neuroblastoma [[cite:PUB00158896], [cite:PUB00158897]]. NOL4L effects gene expression in the PI3K/AKT pathway and is critical for tumor progression and metastasis in ovarian cancer cells [[cite:PUB00158895]].</p>",
